# A note made from the menu, then a task another program writes right after: the agenda
# shows the task once. The core reads the new note inside the create, so the agenda hears
# no reset; when a reset and the change came together, it queried, found the new task
# already there, and then added it a second time.
size 140x30
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
env COLD_LAVA_TODAY=2026-11-07
wait-for example-workspace
keys A
wait-for ↑↓ move · x tick · ⏎ open
expect-not ▾ Today
keys g j enter
wait-for Ctrl-o ⟵ agenda
keys n
wait-for new note in Journal/ · ⏎ create · Esc cancel
type Ash fall
keys enter
wait-for created Journal/Ash fall.md
write Inbox/Chores.md - [ ] Sweep the ash off the roof 📅 2026-11-07\n
keys ctrl+o
wait-for Ctrl-o ⟵ agenda
keys ctrl+o
wait-for ▾ Today · Sat 7 Nov  1
expect ☐ Sweep the ash off the roof
screen
keys q q
exits 0
